    {
      "body": "> What FA version gets run on pre-ampere?\r\n\r\nThanks for taking a look! On pre-Ampere, no FA version runs. `FlashAttentionBackend.supports_compute_capability()` requires SM80+, and FlashInfer is currently gated to SM80+ too, so the selector falls back to Triton. From a T4 (SM75) run on stock v0.33.0:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR [fa_utils.py:212] Cannot use FA version 2 is not supported due to FA2 is only supported on devices with compute capability >= 8\r\nINFO  [cuda.py:508] Using TRITON_ATTN attention backend out of potential backends: ['TRITON_ATTN', 'FLEX_ATTENTION'].\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe ERROR comes from helper checks that still call `get_flash_attn_version()` during setup. It defaults to FA2, finds FA2 unsupported, logs, and returns `None` through the caught `AssertionError`, so it refers to a version that would never be used. For comparison, the FlashInfer sampler handles the same situation on this GPU as a warning: `FlashInfer top-p/top-k sampling unavailable: unsupported compute capability 7.5; falling back.`\r\n\r\nIf you'd prefer, I can instead make `get_flash_attn_version()` return `None` early (without logging) when the device capability is below 8.0, so nothing is logged on these GPUs. I'm happy to go either way.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:12:17Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63592#issuecomment-6589769038",
      "id": 6589769038,
      "updated_at": "2026-11-02T22:13:18Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Raghu-dev-pixel"
      }
    }
  ],
